---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Best Seasons for Traditional Wear Travel | ChinaStyle"
  description="When to visit China for Hanfu photoshoots and qipao tailoring. Best months for each city, seasonal styling tips, and Chinese holidays to avoid when planning."
  canonicalUrl="/plan-trip/seasons"
  articleDate="2026-08-03"
  breadcrumbs={{ name: "Home", url: "/" }, { name: "Plan Your Trip", url: "/plan-trip/" }, { name: "Best Seasons", url: "/plan-trip/seasons/" }}>
  <section class="pt-24 pb-16"><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#b5343a] tracking-[0.15em] uppercase">Plan Your Trip · Seasons</span>
    <h1 class="font-serif-sc text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-stone-900 mt-3">When to Go: Best Seasons for Each City</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-stone-500 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">The season you visit matters for comfort, photos, and whether you''ll be shooting in golden autumn light or sweating through summer silk.</p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-10">
      <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-200 rounded-xl p-5"><h3 class="font-semibold text-green-800">Spring (March-May)</h3><p class="text-xs text-green-700 mt-1.5">Best overall. 15-25dC. Cherry blossoms in Xi''an, peonies in Luoyang, West Lake willows in Hangzhou. Avoid Labor Day (May 1-5).</p></div>
      <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-5"><h3 class="font-semibold text-amber-800">Autumn (Sept-Nov)</h3><p class="text-xs text-amber-700 mt-1.5">Second best. Clear skies, golden light. Xi''an city wall at sunset in October is the best Hanfu photo condition. Avoid National Day (Oct 1-7).</p></div>
      <div class="bg-sky-50 border border-sky-200 rounded-xl p-5"><h3 class="font-semibold text-sky-800">Summer (June-Aug)</h3><p class="text-xs text-sky-700 mt-1.5">Hot 30-38dC. Tang ruqun is lightweight. Shoot mornings only. School holiday crowds July-Aug.</p></div>
      <div class="bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-5"><h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-800">Winter (Dec-Feb)</h3><p class="text-xs text-slate-700 mt-1.5">Cold but empty sites. Ming aoqun layers well. CNY closes businesses 3-5 days but festive atmosphere is magical.</p></div>
    </div>
    <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-14 mb-4">City-by-City Best Months</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse"><thead><tr class="border-b border-stone-200 text-left"><th class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold">City</th><th class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold">Best</th><th class="py-3 font-semibold">Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Xi''an</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Apr, May, Oct</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs">Cherry blossoms on city wall in April; golden autumn light in October</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Beijing</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Apr, May, Sept, Oct</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs">Red leaves + dark tang suits in autumn; Forbidden City best against blue skies</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Shanghai</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Mar-May, Oct-Nov</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs">Plane trees leaf out April; pastel qipao + tree-lined streets</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Suzhou</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Mar-May</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs">Gardens in full bloom; silk qipao against wisteria in April</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Hangzhou</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Mar-Apr, Oct</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs">West Lake willows greenest in March; Song hanfu elegance</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
        <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-14 mb-4">Month-by-Month Guide</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse"><thead><tr class="border-b border-stone-200 text-left"><th class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold">Month</th><th class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold">Best For</th><th class="py-3 font-semibold">Avg Temp</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium">January</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 text-xs">Snow Hanfu photos in Xi'an and Beijing — stunning contrast</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs">-5 to 5°C</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium">February</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 text-xs">Spring Festival (varies) — Tang suit photos in festive Beijing</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs">0 to 10°C</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium">March</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 text-xs">Suzhou gardens begin blooming — silk qipao photos</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs">8 to 18°C</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium">April</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 text-xs">Hanfu Culture Festival in Xi'an + Luoyang peony season</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs">12 to 22°C</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium">May</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 text-xs">Ideal everywhere — warm but not hot, clear skies</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs">18 to 28°C</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium">June</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 text-xs">Guizhou Miao festivals begin — ethnic minority experiences</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs">22 to 32°C</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium">July</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 text-xs">Hangzhou lotus season — light Song dynasty Hanfu by West Lake</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs">26 to 35°C</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium">August</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 text-xs">Evening photoshoots only — too hot for midday costumes</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs">26 to 35°C</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium">September</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 text-xs">Perfect month — Mid-Autumn Festival, clear autumn light</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs">20 to 28°C</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium">October</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 text-xs">Golden Week first week: AVOID. Rest of Oct: Excellent</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs">12 to 22°C</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium">November</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 text-xs">Nanjing autumn leaves — Ming dynasty Hanfu in red forests</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs">5 to 15°C</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium">December</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 text-xs">Moody winter shots, fewer tourists, lower hotel prices</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs">-2 to 8°C</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
    <p class="text-xs text-stone-400 mt-3">Temperatures are approximate ranges for northern cities (Beijing, Xi'an). Southern cities (Shanghai, Hangzhou, Guizhou) are typically 5-8°C warmer.</p>
    
    <div class="mt-8"><a href="/plan-trip" class="text-sm text-stone-400 hover:text-stone-600 transition-colors">Back to Plan Your Trip</a></div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
